  "comments": "<p>Different Obverse and Reverse dies are known.<br><br><i>Obverse</i><br>Die <strong>1</strong> - details smaller, ESCUDOS far from rim, E.VAZ INCM close to rim.<br>Die <strong>2</strong> - details a bit larger, ESCUDOS far from rim, E.VAZ INCM far from rim.<br>Die <strong>3</strong> - details larger, ESCUDOS close to rim, E.VAZ INCM far from rim.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6166b80a3e186.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6166b80a3e186.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br><i>Reverse</i><br>Die <strong>A</strong> - details smaller, top pointer short, inner cross in Order of Christ Cross small.<br>Die <strong>B</strong> - details larger, top pointer long, inner cross in Order of Christ Cross long.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6166b8261e27b.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6166b8261e27b.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br><i>Combinations</i><br><strong>1</strong>+<strong>A</strong>: 1986, 1987.<br><strong>2</strong>+<strong>B</strong>: 1988-1997.<br><strong>3</strong>+<strong>B</strong>: 1998-2001.<br><br>Correspondence to Standard Catalog of World Coins<br>KM#634.1: 1+A, 2+B.<br>KM#634.2: 3+B.</p>",
